      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you -- fixed.\n\nWhen createdir is set, mdcache_openattr now clears MDCACHE_TRUST_ATTRS on the object, so the next GETATTR refreshes it. Creating the directory can change the object\u0027s named_attr and ctime.\n\nWith FSAL_VFS nothing changes on disk when the directory is created. The directory exists exactly when the file has user xattrs. Changes to the named attributes themselves already invalidate the object through an upcall in the VFS backend. But MDCACHE shouldn\u0027t depend on how one FSAL does it.\n\nI cleared the flag instead of calling mdcache_refresh_attrs_no_invalidate(), so a create doesn\u0027t cost an extra getattr. mdcache_link does the same for the linked object. Cached dirents aren\u0027t affected, because MDCACHE only invalidates them when mtime changes.",
      "parentUuid": "1971547e_42299403",
      "revId": "bfd1601685d309922c4a494a837a5dd81767e53a",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
