      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you -- fixed.\n\nIf the directory has to be created and the export doesn\u0027t have EXPORT_OPTION_MD_WRITE_ACCESS, OPENATTR now returns NFS4ERR_ROFS. The check only applies when creation is needed. OPENATTR with createdir set still opens an existing attribute directory on a read-only export.\n\nCreating a named attribute inside the directory is OPEN with OPEN4_CREATE, so the existing check in nfs4_op_open() already covers it.\n\n I tested it with a small script on pynfs\u0027s client library that sends OPENATTR directly, since pynfs has no OPENATTR tests. It covered a read-only and a read-write VFS export, with createdir set and cleared, on files with and without xattrs. The only change from the previous patch set is on the read-only export, for a file without xattrs with createdir set. That now returns NFS4ERR_ROFS instead of NFS4_OK.",
